bugymetaballs-by-lordcow for Debian
-----------------------------------

The orig tarball contains the files of the 4k source compo entry, as
published on https://320x200.org/2004/4k/ : buggy_metaballs.cpp, g.h,
GNUmakefile and file_id.diz.

Part of the data (metaball tables, scroll text, music) is encoded in the
whitespace of buggy_metaballs.cpp: do not reformat or reindent this file,
and keep the patches minimal.

Patches (debian/patches):
 01  replace the GNUmakefile by a Makefile using pkg-config and the
     dpkg-buildflags (CPPFLAGS, CXXFLAGS, LDFLAGS)
 02  start in a window instead of fullscreen
 03  include the SDL 1.2 headers by their full path
 04  add the missing "return *this" of the vector assignment operator: with
     current GCC the intro crashed (SIGILL/SIGSEGV) at start-up
 05  also quit on SDL_QUIT (window close button, SIGTERM)
 06  cap the frame rate to 60 fps (BUGY_FPS): without it the intro ran at
     thousands of frames per second on current hardware

Written by Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>, reviewed by Nicolas HOUDELOT.

